* Pre-Commit Hooks: The First Gate
// From: book_AI_Software_Engineering/lectures_source/Tools_source.smd:983 '* Pre-Commit Hooks'
// From: helpers_root/papers/AIgentic_Development_System/part1.code_quality.tex:401 '\subsubsection{Enforced Checks}'
// From: helpers_root/docs/tools/git/all.git_hooks.how_to_guide.md:44 '## Commit changes'

::: columns
:::: {.column width=60%}
- @Definition@: a **git hook** is a script that Git runs around an event, e.g.,
  a commit, and a failed check aborts the commit

- @Examples@: the checks of `pre-commit.py`
  - `check_master`: no commit on `master`
  - `check_author`: user name and email are set
  - `check_file_size`: no file above 512 KB
  - `check_python_compile`: each changed file compiles
  - `check_gitleaks`: no secret in the staged diff

- @Remark@: `setenv.sh` installs the hooks, and `git commit --no-verify` skips
  them

- @Key idea@: a check of seconds runs on every commit, an agent's included
::::
:::: {.column width=40%}

```bash
> git commit -m "Lint"
'check_master' passed
'check_author' passed
max file size=512 KB
'check_file_size' passed
'check_python_compile'
  passed
'check_gitleaks' passed
All pre-commit hooks
  passed: committing
```

::::
:::

* Running the Formatter After Every Agent Edit
// From: website/docs/blog/posts/draft.how_to.Create_Hook_To_Run_Ruff_In_Claude_Code.md:2 'title: "How to Create a Hook to Run Ruff in Claude Code"'

- @Problem@: an agent edits many files before its first commit, so lints pile
  up until the pre-commit hook rejects them all at once

- @Solution@: a `PostToolUse` hook runs a formatter on each file right after the
  agent writes it _(Anthropic, 2026)_
  ```json
  {"hooks": {"PostToolUse": [{
    "matcher": "Edit|Write",
    "hooks": [{"type": "command",
      "command": "jq -r '.tool_input.file_path' | xargs ruff format"}]
  }]}}
  ```
  - `jq` extracts the path of the edited file from the JSON on stdin

// TODO(gp): Check that a `PostToolUse` hook that exits with code 2 sends its
// stderr back to the model: it is recalled from memory and is not in the notes
- @Remark@: a non-modifying check in the same hook can return its lints to the
  agent as the next input

- @Key idea@: check at the moment of the edit, when the fix is cheapest and the
  context is still loaded

* Checking in CI That the Linter Ran
// From: helpers_root/docs/build_system/all.linter_gh_workflow.explanation.md:1 '# Overview'
// From: helpers_root/docs/build_system/all.linter_gh_workflow.explanation.md:22 '## Run the Linter and Check the Linter Results'

::: columns
:::: {.column width=58%}
- @Problem@: hooks run on the machine of the developer, and `--no-verify` skips
  them

- @Solution@: the `linter.yml` workflow reruns the linter on each PR, with
  `invoke lint_check_if_it_was_run`
  1. Fetch `master`
  2. Run `invoke lint --branch`
  3. Check `git status`
  4. Fail the PR if the tree is dirty

- @Intuition@: the modifying actions leave clean code unchanged, so any diff
  shows that the linter did not run

- @Key idea@: CI does not trust the local gates, it reruns them
::::
:::: {.column width=42%}

```graphviz
digraph LintCheck {
    bgcolor="transparent";
    pad="0.15";
    splines=spline;
    nodesep=0.30;
    ranksep=0.30;
    rankdir=TB;

    node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", penwidth=1.6,
          fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11, margin="0.14,0.07",
          height=0.38];
    edge [color="#A3B1C0", penwidth=1.3, arrowhead=vee, arrowsize=0.7,
          fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fontcolor="#7B8794"];

    // input : orange | process : teal | pass : green | fail : coral

    PR    [label="PR branch",
           fillcolor="#FBEBD4", color="#D9A85F", fontcolor="#6B4517"];
    Lint  [label="invoke lint --branch",
           fillcolor="#B7DDD0", color="#6FA890", fontcolor="#1F4E39"];
    Clean [label="Tree clean?", shape=diamond, style="filled",
           fillcolor="#FFFFFF", color="#9AA9B8", fontcolor="#243B53"];
    Pass  [label="Check passes",
           fillcolor="#DFEDE0", color="#8FB79A", fontcolor="#2E5A3D"];
    Fail  [label="Check fails",
           fillcolor="#F6C6C6", color="#D98C8C", fontcolor="#6B2A2A"];

    PR -> Lint -> Clean;
    Clean -> Pass [label="  Yes"];
    Clean -> Fail [label="  No"];
}
```
